Coalesce redundant native paint events on composited screens

Raising or uncovering an editor window makes the window system deliver a
burst of a dozen or more paint events within a second. Each one was
answered with an unconditional render and present of a view that had not
changed. Servers that throttle presentation of obscured windows complete
each such present from a fallback timer -- Xwayland's runs at 1 Hz -- so
during an editor switch the burst serializes into many one-second waits
on the shared UI thread, freezing both editors for 5-11 s on a large
design.

Two changes:

- onPaint answers a paint event with the clean-view-skippable repaint
  when the screen is composited and a frame finished presenting less
  than 150 ms ago. A dirty view still renders. Non-composited servers
  keep the unconditional repaint, because exposed areas there are
  genuinely lost.

- The refresh timer exists to complete rate-limited Refresh() calls,
  but repainted unconditionally where an undeferred Refresh() skips a
  clean view. It now uses the same skippable path, so deferring a
  refresh no longer strengthens it.

Adds KIPLATFORM::UI::IsScreenComposited (gdk_screen_is_composited on
GTK; always true on MSW and macOS, whose window servers always
composite).

diff --git a/common/draw_panel_gal.cpp b/common/draw_panel_gal.cpp
index e2764da4f6..d6ea7d51d4 100644
--- a/common/draw_panel_gal.cpp
+++ b/common/draw_panel_gal.cpp
@@ -194,7 +194,21 @@ void EDA_DRAW_PANEL_GAL::SetFocus()
 
 void EDA_DRAW_PANEL_GAL::onPaint( wxPaintEvent& WXUNUSED( aEvent ) )
 {
-    DoRePaint( false );
+    // Window systems deliver bursts of paint events when a window is raised or
+    // uncovered. When the view has not changed, rendering for each of them
+    // presents an identical frame, and a server that throttles presentation of
+    // obscured windows can block the UI thread for up to a second per present,
+    // turning one window raise into a multi-second freeze. On a composited
+    // screen the window system retains the presented frame, so a paint event
+    // arriving on the heels of a completed repaint can take the skippable
+    // path, which still renders whenever the view is dirty. Non-composited
+    // servers keep the unconditional repaint: exposed areas there are
+    // genuinely lost and must be redrawn.
+    wxLongLong sinceLastRepaint = wxGetLocalTimeMillis() - m_lastRepaintEnd;
+
+    bool allowSkip = sinceLastRepaint < 150 && KIPLATFORM::UI::IsScreenComposited( this );
+
+    DoRePaint( allowSkip );
 }
 
 
@@ -758,7 +772,21 @@ void EDA_DRAW_PANEL_GAL::onIdle( wxIdleEvent& aEvent )
 
 void EDA_DRAW_PANEL_GAL::onRefreshTimer( wxTimerEvent& aEvent )
 {
-    ForceRefresh();
+    if( !m_drawingEnabled )
+    {
+        // ForceRefresh carries the GAL bootstrap: it attaches the paint
+        // handlers once the backend is ready, or re-arms this timer to try
+        // again.
+        ForceRefresh();
+        return;
+    }
+
+    // This timer completes rate-limited Refresh() calls, so it must repaint
+    // with the same clean-view skip an immediate Refresh() uses. Escalating
+    // to an unconditional repaint would turn every deferred refresh of an
+    // unchanged view into a full render.
+    if( !DoRePaint() )
+        RequestRefresh();
 }
 
 
